   25: 
   26: ## Acceptance volume + incumbent-boundary FDR estimate
   27: - tested accepted by HAND boundary: 10,951; decoy-side accepted: 0; population ratio 2.04 -> point estimate FDR = 0.00%. With 0 of 5,536,655 null acceptances, the one-sided 95% bound is <= 0.056% of hand-accepted pairs (rule-of-three x ratio). This bounds CHANCE-alignment errors only ג€” it is a different (narrower) error class than human semantic grading.
   28: - BH q=0.01: accepted 96,548 tested pairs (p-cut 8.54e-05)
   29: - BH q=0.05: accepted 160,324 tested pairs (p-cut 7.07e-04)
   30: 
   31: ## Tier-1 ground-truth recall (pairs present in probe corpus)
   32: | family | GT pairs | as candidates | hand | q=0.01 | q=0.05 |
   33: |---|---|---|---|---|---|
   34: | joins | 36 | 36 | 35 | 36 | 36 |
   35: | titles | 1866 | 1866 | 1829 | 1866 | 1866 |
   36: | bh | 118 | 118 | 114 | 118 | 118 |
   37: 
   38: ## Per-stratum null sensitivity (same-bucket null pairs; median/q05)
   39: | bucket | [25,50) | [50,100) | [100,200) | [200,400) | [400,800) | 800+ |
   40: |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
   41: | background | 0.783/0.688 | 0.776/0.713 | 0.761/0.708 | 0.781/0.741 | 0.793/0.764 | 0.800/0.778 |
   42: | titles | 0.767/0.674 | 0.773/0.711 | 0.754/0.698 | 0.774/0.728 | 0.788/0.751 | 0.800/0.774 |
   43: | bh | 0.773/0.647 | 0.742/0.667 | 0.720/0.653 | 0.750/0.693 | 0.777/0.735 | 0.787/0.776 |
   44: | joins | ג€” | 0.776/0.716 | 0.760/0.715 | 0.781/0.745 | 0.792/0.767 | 0.797/0.778 |
   45: 
   46: ## Chunk-size sensitivity (Codex review HIGH-1) ג€” orchestrator synthesis
   47: 
   48: The decoy design has two opposing biases: small chunks (CHUNK=10) destroy every
   49: k-gram crossing a chunk boundary (decoys less phrase-like -> null too HIGH ->
   50: thresholds too loose); large chunks (CHUNK=25) leave intact 25-letter runs of
   51: REAL text in the decoys (genuine short matches counted as null -> null lower
   52: tail too LOW -> thresholds too tight). The rerun at CHUNK=25
   53: (`a5_conformal_fdr_report_c25.md`) shows the effect is material at q=0.01:
   54: 
   55: | bin | hand | q=0.01 (c10, optimistic) | q=0.01 (c25, conservative) |
   56: |---|---|---|---|
   57: | [50,100) | 0.300 | 0.596 | 0.374 |
   58: | [100,200) | 0.386 | 0.576 | 0.396 |
   59: | [200,400) | 0.418 | 0.648 | 0.469 |
   60: | [400,800) | 0.418 | 0.690 | 0.572 |
   61: | 800+ | 0.418 | 0.714 | 0.662 |
   62: 
   63: **Adopt the conservative envelope (c25).** Even under it, tier-1 recall at
   64: q=0.01 is 36/36 joins, 1,861/1,866 titles, 117/118 BH (hand: 35/1,832/114) ג€”
   65: i.e. a modest, principled relaxation (~0.30-0.42 -> ~0.37-0.66 by length)
   66: captures essentially all known ground truth at bounded chance-FDR. Notably the
   67: c25 thresholds land almost exactly where the liturgy-connectivity evidence
   68: pointed during the probe (density ~0.45): the two independent lines agree.
   69: Wave-2 refinement: a leak-free decoy (e.g. chunk-shuffle with chunk-boundary
   70: gram EXCLUSION on the real side too, or cross-page chimeras with provenance
   71: tracking) can narrow the c10/c25 bracket.
   72: 
   73: ## Graded-pairs overlap
   74: - pages from Hillel's 164 graded pairs present in probe corpus: 278 (grades were taken at rehearsal/full scale; full validation belongs to the wave-2 calibration)
   75: 
   76: ## Caveats / wave-2 plan
   77: - DF inflation: decoys add ~25% pages -> DF cap slightly stricter than production. Wave-2: two-run protocol (clean run for tested pairs, decoy run for the null), on liturgy.db then fullcorpus.db behind the compute queue.
   78: - ~2% duplicate candidate rows not deduped (matches candidate_pairs vs candidate_unique_pairs at rehearsal scale).
   79: - Single-chunk residual leak bounded by CHUNK=10 (span is mostly margin -> density >> any threshold).
   80: - Exchangeability argument: decoy candidates traverse the identical seed/DF/two-hit/verify path as tested candidates; the null is conditioned on candidate-generation by construction.
   81: 
   82: Total runtime: 309s.

